## 13. Future Improvements

The application could be improved in the future by adding user accounts, saving multiple trip plans, drag-and-drop trip list ordering, route planning between selected places, more advanced rating-based sorting, mobile interface improvements, and exporting the trip list as a PDF or text file.

## 14. Conclusion

Travel Planner successfully meets the main goals of the Problem Solving project. It allows users to search for places using public APIs, view a clear list of results, add and remove places from a personal trip list, and save the list using LocalStorage.

The project also includes optional features such as category filtering, distance sorting, custom place creation, map integration, search caching, and basic testing.

Overall, the application demonstrates practical use of frontend technologies, API integration, data management, and user-centered design.
